<title>GERMANY: Thyssen to make statement on Transrapid.</title>
<headline>Thyssen to make statement on Transrapid.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thyssen AG, main private-sector backer of the controversial Transrapid high-speed rail project, will make a statement on the project at midday, a Thyssen spokeswoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Sueddeutsche Zeitung reported earlier that construction firms Phillip Holzmann, Hochtief and Bilfinger + Berger planned to withdraw from the project, but the builders said the project would continue without them.</p>
<p>Transportation Minister Matthias Wissmann will also give a news conference with private-sector representatives at 0830 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
